  "label": "About the Author",
  "title": "ABOUT THE AUTHOR",
  "shortTitle": "ABOUT THE AUTHOR",
  "sourceRange": [
    681,
    694
  ],
  "headerSourceParagraphs": {
    "title": 681
  },
  "elements": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Lalit R. Mishra is the creator of The Human Fiction series."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 682
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He writes from observation, not ideology."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 683
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "From watching how thought builds identity, how meaning attaches itself to experience, and how a “self” is continuously constructed through narrative."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 684
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "His central question is simple:"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 685
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Why does experience feel like it is happening to someone?"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 686
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "His work does not aim to provide answers or beliefs."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 687
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It aims to make the structure of thinking visible."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 688
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "In his view, clarity is not something added to life."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 689
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It appears when unnecessary interpretation quiets down."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 690
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "The Human Fiction is not a philosophy to follow."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 691
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It is an exploration of how human experience becomes a story — and how that story is mistaken for reality."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 692
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He does not claim authority over truth."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 693
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He only points toward the process through which truth is interpreted."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 694
    }
  ],
  "index": 21,
  "suppressHeaderNumber": true,
